{title: The Belt and The Famine}
{subtitle: Acts 11:27–30; 21:10–14}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Prophets came [Bb/D]down to Antioch [Cm7]town
From Je[Ab]rusalem [Bb]where the story's [Eb]known
One stood up [Bb/D]named A[Cm7]gabus there
By the [Ab]Spirit he made [Bb]a declara[Eb]tion
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Abmaj7]A severe famine over the whole [Bb]world
[Abmaj7]In the days of Claudius [Bb]it unfurled
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]He warned of the [Bb]hunger that would [Cm7]come
[Eb]He warned of the [Bb]binding to be [Cm7]done
The [Ab]Spirit [Bb]spoke through the [Eb]prophet’s [Bb/D][Cm7]voice
[Ab]To show the [Bb]path of the man’s [Eb]choice
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Disciples decid[Bb/D]ed to send re[Cm7]lief
Each ac[Ab]cording to [Bb]their abili[Eb]ty
To broth[Bb/D]ers living in [Cm7]Judea’s land
[Ab]Barnabas and [Bb]Saul carried the [Eb]plan
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Abmaj7]Then in Caesarea the days went [Bb]by
[Abmaj7]A prophet came down from [Bb]Judea nigh
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At Philip’s [Bb/D]house he took Paul’s [Cm7]belt
[Ab]Tied his own hands [Bb]and feet by the [Eb]text
Said the Jews in Jeru[Bb/D]salem would [Cm7]bind
